xt stage's transport does not exist, and that is now measured rather than assumed.** No `gscript` verb, no `Op*.vi`, and none of the 50 erdosmiller `Create*.vi` files creates a Local Variable; the external fact search adds the reason it cannot be faked — `Control → Create:Local Variable` **6331C02** takes *no parameters*, so the control instance **is** the binding, and `build_invoke` (whose `reference` is deliberately unwired) can never address one. So S3b gets one op VI, `OpCreateLocal_v0`, authorised by **46(k)** — Pre-decided 2 forbids another *process device*, not an op VI — with its design fixed in the plan so no material session improvises it, and the stage cut into five saved sub-steps (`Pre-decided 49`). I deliberately inverted NEXT's order: the locals are created and wired **before** the node moves, because those two steps are each savable at `ExecState` 1 while the moves are what breaks the VI — which is exactly how cycle 54 ended with nothing on disk.\n\n**Two reviews disposed, both by me.** Cycle 58's retrospective named `guard_cycle`'s retrospective gate as a failed device, claiming *\"no ordering, no repair, and no honesty can ever launch a recipe mid-cycle\"* — **refuted by this cycle's own record**: the launch succeeded first try, and the reviewer's counterfactual (\"S3a on disk by ~02:15\") came true at ~02:11, one session boundary later. Its true half — the gate's stderr names \"the previous cycle\" while its condition is \"any newer build log\" — is kept as the standing sequencing rule. `docs/violation-decisions.md` carries the dated `no-device` block (02:34, real `HH:MM`, per 48(l)). Cycle 59's own retrospective returned **`VIOLATION: none`** — the first in the record — and is disposed.\n\n**Three things I could not finish, all in `## NEXT`:** the `git commit` was refused (`git` is not on this non-interactive session's allowlist), so the cycle's files are on disk uncommitted; a one-line repair to `tools/retrospective.py`'s plan-name resolution is